        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add plan-first Claw status and remove",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add experimental `claws status [claw-or-agent]` with canonical agent, workspace-file, package, session, and scheduled-job state\n- bind `claws remove` consent to a dry-run `planIntegrity` digest and revalidate the complete removal surface before mutation\n- recover and expose orphaned subordinate provenance even when the root install row or agent config is missing\n- serialize package lifecycle mutations across processes; skill mutations are serialized per workspace because they share one ClawHub lockfile\n- treat plugins as global: Claw removal releases plugin references but does not uninstall the plugin; workspace-scoped skills remain eligible for safe final-reference removal\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is the status/remove slice for the grouped one-Claw/one-agent contract. Package names resolve an install only when unambiguous; final agent ids always work and disambiguate repeated adds.\n\nRemove is plan-first. Dry-run binds agent identity and config-removal surfaces, route bindings, agent-to-agent allow entries, scheduled-job blockers, managed-file digests, package ownership, workspace/agent/session cleanup targets, and root install state into `planIntegrity`. Apply requires `--yes --plan-integrity <digest>`, rebuilds the plan, and fails closed if consent-bearing input changed.\n\nMissing managed files are treated as already removed; locally modified or untracked operator files are retained. Canonical workspace, agent-state, and session paths are validated and staged before deletion. Partial cleanup retains subordinate provenance for status/retry rather than inventing a permanent removal tombstone.\n\nPlugins are global OpenClaw resources. Removing a Claw emits an explicit retain reason and releases only that Claw's plugin reference. Skills are workspace-scoped: a final unchanged Claw-installed skill can be removed through the canonical ClawHub skill lifecycle, while shared, adopted, drifted, incomplete, provenance-ambiguous, or otherwise uncertain skills are retained.\n\nAll commands remain gated by `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`, and JSON contracts remain experimental.\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27\n- Depends on: #102228 package installation, ownership, and references\n- This PR: lifecycle visibility and consent-bound cleanup\n- Next: #102306 portable export from the same provenance ledger\n\n## Validation\n\nExact head: `da8e4d41d73c77c6294e8813ac2856ad402a646b`\n\n- 49 focused lifecycle/package/ownership/skill-uninstall unit tests passed\n- targeted canonical ClawHub plugin-install lease test passed\n- real `add -> status -> remove dry-run -> digest-bound remove` CLI E2E passed with the dedicated E2E config\n- scoped TypeScript check: no PR-local errors\n- Oxlint clean across all changed TypeScript files\n- Oxfmt and `git diff --check` clean\n- `codex --dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox review --uncommitted`: no discrete actionable regressions\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n`src/claws/lifecycle.e2e.test.ts` invokes the real `src/entry.ts` CLI in an isolated state directory and passes the complete add, status, removal preview, and digest-bound removal flow. The final result is `openclaw.clawRemoveResult.v1` with `status: \"complete\"`; canonical agent config is removed and the unchanged managed workspace file is deleted.",
